    "description": "<p>With a crunchy bite when raw, rhubarb tastes rather sour, although a better term to describe it would be tart. Its sour and tangy taste is a combination of citrusy sweet fruit sourness of limes and lemons. Its puckery taste resembles the effect of green, unripe apples, prunes, and grapes. Famously known for being delicious in pies!</p>",
